@demographics
new-page: true

= **Demographic Groups**

**Working Class**: The urban working class - blue-collar workers in factories, workshops, mines, and the like. Most are <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span>, supporting either the **[+ spd_name_colour +]** or **[+ uspd_name_colour +]**. They make up 40-50% of the population.

**Old Mittelstand**: The old middle class consists of independent artisans, shopkeepers, and small-time businesspeople. They tend to be conservative and are the strongest base for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>. 10-15% of the population.

**New Mittelstand**: The new middle class consists of white-collar workers and government employees. This is the base of <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberalism</span>. 10-15% of the population.

**Rural**: Small and large farmers and independent rural workers. Protestant farmers usually support the **[+ dnvp_name_colour +]**.

**Catholics** are the largest religious minority, at about 30% of the population. They disproportionately support the <span style="color: #000000;">[+ z_name_english +]</span>

**Jews** account for between 0.5% to 1% of the population, and tend to support liberal parties, [? if ddp_name == "DDP" or not ddp_name: mostly the **[+ ddp_name_colour +]**?][? if ddp_name == "DStP": although the mild antisemitism of the Young German Order and it's association with the **[+ ddp_name_colour +]** has driven them away?], although substantial numbers support the **[+ spd_name_colour +]** or **[+ uspd_name_colour +]**.

