[? if ddp_name == "DDP" : a left-liberal party, popular among the intelligentsia and educated middle class. Although, they have been shifting towards the right over the years, they have often been in coalitions with us. ?][? if ddp_name == "DStP": a liberal party, waning in popularity among the intelligentsia and middle class. ?] 

**[+ z_name_colour +]** - <i>[+ z_name_full_colour +]</i> <span style="color: #000000;">([+ z_name_english +])</span>

Party Leader: [+ z_leader_fullname +]
Party Ideology: [+ z_ideology +]
Current relations: [+ z_relation : relationships +]

A centrist to center-right Catholic party that supports the Republic, and has historically supported many of our labor, welfare, and anti-militarist priorities. They have often been in coalitions with us. They are often associated with the **[+ bvp_name_colour +]** (Bavarian People's Party), which represents Catholics in Bavaria. [? if (year >= 1930 or chancellor == "Brüning") and z_leader == "Kaas": They have appeared to take a more conservative turn recently, with the rise of Brüning and the party leader, Ludwig Kaas. ?][? if (year >= 1930 or chancellor == "Brüning") and z_leader == "Stegerwald": They have appeared to take a more conservative turn recently, with the rise of Brüning and the party leader, Adam Stegerwald, who has taken a focus on interconfessionalizing the party. ?][? if (year >= 1930 or chancellor == "Brüning") and z_leader == "Joos": They have appeared to take a more conservative turn recently, with the rise of Brüning and support of austerity. ?]

**[+ bvp_name_colour +]** <i>[+ bvp_name_full_colour +]</i> ([+ bvp_name_english +]) 

Party Leader: [+ bvp_leader_fullname +]
Party Ideology: [+ bvp_ideology +]
Current relations: [+ bvp_relation : relationships +]

A center-right, fiercely regionalist party which represents Catholics in Bavaria. Closely associated with the [+ z_name_full +], particularly its more conservative elements.

**[+ dvp_name_colour +]** - <i>[+ dvp_name_full_colour +]</i> ([+ dvp_name_english +])

Party Leader: [+ dvp_leader_fullname +]
Party Ideology: [+ dvp_ideology +]
Current relations: [+ dvp_relation : relationships +]

A conservative-liberal party founded by Gustav Stresemann, supported by the middle classes, bourgeoisie and industrialists. The industrial and right wing of the party has been gaining noticeable influence in recent years with Stresemann's neglect of party affairs. We have occasionally been in coalitions.

**[+ dnvp_name_colour +]** - <i>[+ dnvp_name_full_colour +]</i> ([+ dnvp_name_english +]) 

Party Leader: [+ dnvp_leader_fullname +]
Party Ideology: [+ dnvp_ideology +]
Current relations: [+ dnvp_relation : relationships +]

A right-wing nationalist-conservative party, with authoritarian, monarchist, and racist elements. It is supported by the former aristocracy, rural landowners, and conservative Lutherans.

**[+ nsdap_name_colour +]** - </i>[+ nsdap_name_full_colour +]</i> - ([+ nsdap_name_english +], or <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazis</span>) 

Party Leader: [+ nsdap_leader_fullname +]
Party Ideology: [+ nsdap_ideology +]
Current relations: [+ nsdap_relation : relationships +]

A far-right nationalist and antisemitic party. Led by Adolf Hitler, they attempted a coup in 1923, and were banned for it, but have since been legalized.


**Other parties** - there is a multitude of small, mostly conservative parties, such as the Economic Party of the German Middle Class, the Farmer's Party, the Agricultural League, and others.

