@paramilitaries
on-arrival: {!
Q.rb_strength = Math.round(Q.rb_strength);
Q.sh_strength = Math.round(Q.sh_strength);
Q.sa_strength = Math.round(Q.sa_strength); 
Q.rfb_strength = Math.round(Q.rfb_strength); 
!}
new-page: true

= **Paramilitary groups:**

= The [+ rb_name_full_colour +] **([+ rb_name_colour +])**

Strength: [+ rb_strength +] thousand (Militarization: [+ rb_militancy : militancy +]):

The [+ rb_name_full +] is an organization affiliated with all of the democratic parties - the **[+ spd_name_colour +]**, **[+ z_name_colour +]**, and [? if lvp_formed: the former ?]**[+ ddp_name_colour +]**, but primarily with the **[+ spd_name_colour +]**. Historically, this has been an unarmed organization.


= The [+ bw_name_full_colour +] (**[+ bw_name_colour +]**): 

Strength: [+ rfb_strength +] thousand (Militarization: [+ rfb_militancy : militancy +])

The "[+ rfb_name_full +]" is associated with the **[+ uspd_name_colour +]**.


= [+ sh_name_full_colour +] **([+ sh_name_colour +])**:

Strength: [+ sh_strength +] thousand (Militarization: [+ sh_militancy : militancy +])

A right-wing nationalist organization of primarily Great War veterans, descended from the *Freikorps* that emerged after the war. Associated with the **[+ dnvp_name_colour +]**.


= [+ sa_name_full_colour +] **([+ sa_name_colour +])**: 

Strength: [+ sa_strength +] thousand (Militarization: [+ sa_militancy : militancy +])

This is the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Nazi</span> paramilitary group.

**Official military groups:**

**Reichswehr**: 
[+ reichswehr_strength +] thousand troops. (Loyalty: [+ reichswehr_loyalty : loyalty +])

This is Germany's military.

**Prussian police**: 
[+ prussian_police_strength +] thousand members. (Loyalty: [+ prussian_police_loyalty : loyalty +])

The State Police of Prussia.

