@factions

= **Internal factions of the** **[+ spd_name_colour +]**

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**[+ spd_left_colour +]** (Strength: [+ left_strength : strength +] | Dissent: [+ left_dissent : dissent +])

Many leftists are former members of the <span style="color: #D47B9B;">**old USPD**</span> (the left-wing, anti-war <span style="color: #D47B9B;">Independent Social Democratic Party</span>), who came afoul of the leadership, or are young radicals. Many are interested in closer cooperation with the **[+ uspd_name_colour +]**, and some support extra-parliamentary action.

**[+ spd_center_colour +]** (Strength: [+ center_strength : strength +] | Dissent: [+ center_dissent : dissent +])

Centrists in the **[+ spd_name_colour +]** are followers of the doctrine of orthodox <span style="color: #9B0000;">Marxism</span> as expounded by Karl Kautsky and later Rudolf Hilferding. They seek a middle course between reform and revolution, while defending the democratic state.

**[+ spd_labor_colour +]** (Strength: [+ labor_strength : strength +] | Dissent: [+ labor_dissent : dissent +])

Many **[+ spd_name_colour +]** members are also part of the ADGB, the federation of free trade unions. Their goal is economic reform and benefits for organized workers.

**[+ spd_reformist_colour +]** (Strength: [+ reformist_strength : strength +] | Dissent: [+ reformist_dissent : dissent +])

Reformists are pragmatic participants in government, and seek to expand the welfare state and defend democracy against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span>. [? if spd_prussia : They are dominant in the state government of Prussia. ?]

[? if neorevisionism: **[+ spd_neorevisionist_colour +]** (Strength: [+ neorevisionist_strength : strength +] | Dissent: [+ neorevisionist_dissent : dissent +] ?])

[? if neorevisionism: Neorevisionists focus on defending the republic and expanding democracy, while also expanding the party's base beyond the working class to create a people's party. They support new propaganda methods and extra-parliamentary action in defense of the republic. ?]

